From: afni-win
Subject: [PATCH] split PATH at the platform separator in the R programs

Why the compat layer cannot handle this: every AFNI R program (and
AFNIio.R) finds its companion files, e.g. AFNIio.R, with a first.in.path()
that splits the PATH environment variable at ':' in R code. On Windows R
the separator is ';' and every entry starts with a drive letter "C:", so
the split yields no valid directory and the program stops before reading
any data. The R code runs in the R interpreter, outside the C compat layer,
and PATH must stay a valid Windows PATH for R itself. The patch uses
.Platform$path.sep, which is ':' on Linux and macOS, so nothing changes
there. (docs/DECISIONS.md D39)
diff --git a/src/R_scripts/1dGC.R b/src/R_scripts/1dGC.R
index 903443b..0c9e3f8 100644
--- a/src/R_scripts/1dGC.R
+++ b/src/R_scripts/1dGC.R
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ print("        SSCC/NIMH, National Institutes of Health, Bethesda MD 20892")
 print("#+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++")
 
 first.in.path <- function(file) {
-   ff <- paste(strsplit(Sys.getenv('PATH'),':')[[1]],'/', file, sep='')
+   ff <- paste(strsplit(Sys.getenv('PATH'), .Platform$path.sep)[[1]],'/', file, sep='')
    ff<-ff[lapply(ff,file.exists)==TRUE];
    #cat('Using ', ff[1],'\n');
    return(gsub('//','/',ff[1], fixed=TRUE))
